# T0058 — Referencing records within records

**Task:** T0058 — Referencing records within records  
**Branch (on approval):** `T0058-record-references`  
**State:** shipped — finish-up  
**PROD task id:** 65 · projectId 4 · priority medium · state `in_progress`

## QA follow-ups

- Suggestion popup: use rectangular corners (not `--radius-chip` pill/oval).

## Context

Users need to mention other TaskMesh records from the **Markdown editor** via shorthand typeahead (same UX spirit as Depends-on search), then land a clickable markdown link. Also `@` for user display-name mentions (no notifications this phase).

## Size / split

Large but cohesive: display-number schema for many entity types + search API + TipTap suggestion UI + deep-link navigation. **Recommend shipping as one worktask** with ordered milestones below. Split only if implementation stalls mid-flight (e.g. schema/API first as a follow-up task).

## Decisions (confirmed)

1. **Stable display IDs** for all referenceable types (not title-only search for non-task types).
2. **Insert both** bracket-style label **and** a markdown link (clickable).
3. **`#` trigger:** treat line-start `#` as heading territory; mid-line `#` as reference. Implementation nuance (proposed): still allow reference when `#` is followed by a **known type letter** even at line start (so intentional `#T00…` works); suppress when `#` + space / non-type text at line start (Heading1).
4. **Click-through** in preview (and edit when clicking the link).
5. **`@` users:** insert **display name**; notifications later.
6. **Entity coverage:** idea, project, task, document, board, canvas, wiki_node, todo_list, image_board, plus users via `@`.
7. **Suggest threshold:** match Depends-on (`q.length >= 1` after the type letter / after `@`).

