## Goals

- App-wide unique `number` per entity type (same pattern as tasks/users); backfill existing rows; allocate on create.
- Show reference IDs in list/detail chrome where titles already appear (at least ElementShell / common headers) so users learn the codes.
- `GET` reference search API filtered by prefix/type, matching number **or** title (Depends-on logic).
- TipTap `#` / `@` suggestion popovers in `MarkdownEditor` (edit mode only).
- On select: insert markdown link whose **label** is `[T0010] Title` (or `@DisplayName` for users) and **href** is a stable client path.
- Resolve clicks to the right screen (idea page, project tab + entity, task open, image board editor, etc.).
- User `@` mention: plain linked or styled display name; no notification side effects.

## Non-goals

- Notifications / inbox for `@` mentions.
- Autocomplete outside MarkdownEditor (Excalidraw, plain inputs).
- Changing Depends-on search (reuse patterns only).
- Public/share links or cross-instance refs.

## Implementation

### 1. Schema + migration

Add `number integer not null unique` to: `ideas`, `projects`, `project_documents`, `boards`, `canvases`, `wiki_nodes`, `todo_lists`, `image_boards`.

- Backfill each table: assign sequential numbers (by `id` order) starting at 1.
- Create helpers `allocate*Number` (max+1) mirroring `allocateTaskNumber`.
- Wire creates in existing services/routes to allocate numbers.
- Shared formatters: `formatEntityRef(prefix, n)` → `T0010`; client + server `lib` modules.

### 2. Reference search API

`GET /api/v1/references/search?q=…&type=task|idea|…` (or parse type from `q` like `T003` / `003` when `type` set).

- Response: `{ data: [{ entityType, id, number, title, href, projectId? }] }` (limit ~20).
- Number matching: digits, padded display (`T0031`), partial (`003`, `T00`).
- Title `ILIKE` like Depends-on.
- Users: separate path or `type=user` for `@` (search `displayName`; return `referenceId` + name). Prefer a non-admin route so Markdown editor does not need admin APIs.

### 3. Deep links (`href`)

Stable app paths (extend query params where selection is local state today):

| Type | Target |
|------|--------|
| task | `/tasks?open=<id>` (or project tasks tab + open) — open modal/editor |
| idea | `/ideas/:id` |
| project | `/projects/:id` |
| document | `/projects/:pid?tab=documents&doc=:id` |
| board | `/projects/:pid?tab=boards&board=:id` |
| canvas | `/projects/:pid?tab=canvases&canvas=:id` |
| wiki_node | `/projects/:pid?tab=wiki&node=:id` |
| todo_list | `/todos/:id` |
| image_board | `/image-board/:id` |
| user | `/settings/profile` if self, else no-op / admin users later — label only is fine |

Wire ProjectDetailPage (and panels) to honor `doc` / `board` / `canvas` / `node` query params on load.

### 4. MarkdownEditor — `#` and `@` suggestions

- TipTap Suggestion (or lightweight mirror of Depends-on dropdown) for:
  - **`#` + type letter + query** (mid-line, or line-start only when type letter follows).
  - **`@` + name query**.
- Dropdown: small list — **Number + title** (match Depends-on row style); keyboard nav + click.
- On pick entity: replace the trigger text with  
  `[T0010] Title` as a **link** → e.g. `[\[T0010\] Title](/projects/4?tab=documents&doc=12)`  
  (literal visible label includes brackets + number + title).
- On pick user: insert `@DisplayName` (optionally linked); no notification.
- Preview/readOnly: links clickable (existing Link extension); SPA navigation via click handler intercepting internal hrefs when needed.
- Do **not** steal Heading1: line-start `#` + space remains heading.

### 5. Display numbers in UI

Surface `I####` / `P####` / etc. in primary chrome for each entity (list rows / ElementShell `titleLeading`) so the shorthand is discoverable—not a full redesign.

### 6. Tests

- Allocate/backfill uniqueness.
- Search by number token + title.
- Optional: parser for trigger (line-start vs mid-line).

## Out of scope / later

- `@` notifications and activity feed.
- Command-palette parity for the same refs (already has global search).
- Import/export rewriting of refs.

## QA checklist (preview)

After implement, user should verify:

1. Mid-line `#T` / `#I` / … opens typeahead; selecting inserts `[T####] Title` as a working link.
2. Line-start `# ` still creates Heading1; reference does not fire incorrectly.
3. `@` suggests users by name; inserts display name only.
4. Preview click navigates to idea / project / doc / board / canvas / wiki / todo / image board / task.
5. New records get the next number; existing records show stable IDs after migrate.
6. Mobile: suggestion list usable; editor still resizes normally.
